.TITLE "touch"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Updates file access and modification times. It can also be used to create new __empty files__ if the specified path does not already exist.

.DIV "TLDR"
**touch file.txt**
Updates the access and modification times to the current time, or creates an empty file.
> __file.txt__ target file

**touch -t YYYYMMDDhhmm file.txt**
Sets a specific timestamp for a file's modification and access time.
> __-t__ timestamp flag | __YYYYMMDDhhmm__ the date and time

**touch -a file.txt**
Updates only the access time of a file.
> __-a__ access time flag

**touch -m file.txt**
Updates only the modification time of a file.
> __-m__ modification time flag

**touch -r reference.txt file.txt**
Applies the timestamps of a reference file to another file.
> __-r__ reference flag | __reference.txt__ source file | __file.txt__ target file

.DIV "SUMMARY"
The __touch__ command is a quick and non-destructive way to signal that a file has been "worked on," which is often used by build systems and automation scripts.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:ls**

